q(1975,6,'Combinatorics',r'Fifteen guests sit around a circular table with fifteen equally spaced name cards. (i) If initially no guest is at their own card, prove some rotation of the table places at least two guests correctly. (ii) Give an initial arrangement with exactly one guest correct such that no rotation places more than one correctly.','Pigeonhole principle|Permutations & arrangements|Algorithms & constructions')
